description: Avoid en/em dashes in written text; use hyphens or rephrase
alwaysApply: true
---

# No en/em dashes in text

Never use en dashes (`–`, U+2013) or em dashes (`—`, U+2014) in copy, UI strings, comments, commit messages, or documentation.

Prefer:

- A hyphen with spaces: `homepage - pricing - about`
- A comma, colon, or parentheses: `homepage, pricing, about`
- A rewrite that needs no dash: `four core pages: homepage, pricing, about, and contact`

```text
❌ Before — after contrast using live captures
✅ Before / after contrast using live captures
✅ Before-after contrast using live captures

❌ Website redesign — homepage, pricing, about
✅ Website redesign: homepage, pricing, about
```

ASCII hyphen-minus (`-`) is fine for compound words (`science-backed`) and ranges when needed (`2023-2024`).
